+# Speck Feedback — Missing product-contract path falsely passes validation
+
+**Date**: 2026-08-10  
+**Speck version (workspace)**: v10.5.0  
+**Repo HEAD**: `b627b32` on branch `master`  
+**Workspace**: `001-pulseboard` (build; S008 audit)
+
+## TL;DR
+
+`validate-product-contract.sh --strict` returned exit status `0` with no output when passed the nonexistent path `specs/projects/001-pulseboard/product-contract.md`. The sibling banned-language and gate-liveness gates correctly reported the missing contract. No methodology patch was applied.
+
+## Gap / Observation F1: Explicit missing product-contract path is accepted
+
+**Symptom**: The command below produced no diagnostic and exited `0`:
+
+```text
+bash .speck/scripts/validation/validators/validate-product-contract.sh --strict specs/projects/001-pulseboard/product-contract.md
+```
+
+**Reproduction**:
+
+1. Use a workspace with no `product-contract.md` at the supplied path.
+2. Run the command above.
+3. Observe exit status `0`.
+
+**Root cause**: `validate-product-contract.sh` does not reject a nonexistent explicit target before its content checks.
+
+**Severity**: P1
+
+**Patch applied**: none — reported through this feedback artifact.
+
+**Proposed upstream fix**: Validate that the supplied path exists and is a regular file before parsing; emit a named non-zero failure such as `PRODUCT_CONTRACT_MISSING.P1`.
+
+**Impact**: An audit can receive a green product-contract verdict even though the contract is absent, which manufactures false evidence.
+
+## Concrete proposals summary (prioritized)
+
+| # | Proposal | Effort | Impact |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| **P1** | Reject nonexistent explicit product-contract paths. | Small | Removes a false-green audit gate. |
